Package: orange-pi-terminal
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 libc6, libstdc++6, libgcc-s1, libsqlcipher0 [arm64], libmbedcrypto7 [arm64],
 nodejs, python3, python3-cryptography, python3-pil,
 nftables, polkitd, pulseaudio-utils,
 libvlc5, vlc-plugin-base,
 openjdk-17-jdk-headless,
 ffmpeg
Recommends: gstreamer1.0-plugins-base, gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-bad, gstreamer1.0-plugins-ugly, gstreamer1.0-libav
Description: Modular terminal for Raspberry Pi with ESP32 module support
 Qt 6 based kiosk terminal for the Raspberry Pi. Provides the UI,
 the PBR1 serial control plane, BLE/LAN business transport, per-user
 encrypted storage (SQLCipher), module sandboxing through systemd
 DynamicUser workers, and a default-deny network egress policy.
 .
 The package bundles its own Qt 6.5.3 runtime under /opt/orange-pi-terminal
 so the target image does not need a matching system Qt.

Package: orange-pi-terminal-dev
Architecture: any
Depends: orange-pi-terminal (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Section: libdevel
Description: Module SDK for orange-pi-terminal
 Headers and CMake package files needed to build native modules for the
 terminal: pi_module_api.h, IModulePlugin.h and OrangePiModuleSDKConfig.cmake.
 .
 Install this package on a development machine or on the target when
 building modules on-device.
